+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+`ToolRegistry.execute` validates `input` against the resolved tool definition's `inputSchema` before the executor runs. A rejection is returned as a `ToolResponse`, so the model can read it and correct the call within the tool-round budget; only an unknown tool name throws.
+
+## Validation
+
+- Input missing a required property is answered with a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names the property, and the executor is never invoked ([validated by: rejects input missing a required property with a result naming it, and never runs the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L42)).
+- Valid input carrying an unlisted extra property reaches the executor unchanged, exactly once ([validated by: passes valid input with an unlisted extra property to the executor unchanged, exactly once](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L53)).
+- A wrong-typed field is rejected with a message naming its path and expected type, and neither the message nor any log line contains the offending value ([validated by: rejects a wrong-typed field naming its path and expected type, and leaks its value nowhere](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L66)).
+- `register` throws for an uncompilable schema, and the message names the tool ([validated by: throws at register time for an uncompilable schema, naming the tool](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L80)).
+- A function-valued definition is validated against the schema it returns at that call, not a stale one ([validated by: validates a function-valued definition against the schema current at that call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L86)).
